2026-10-25T02:36:54.5961480Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6531670Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6556630Z [0m
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6558210Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6558670Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6558920Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6559140Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6559550Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6561240Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6561600Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6562030Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6562760Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6563120Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [351..356])[0m and groups [34m(gid 350)[0m
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6565290Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6566820Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6568380Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6568580Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6568760Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6569030Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6569210Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6569570Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6569730Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6570190Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6570370Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6570740Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6571180Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6583810Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6585080Z I will:
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6585390Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6585760Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6586630Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6587530Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6589390Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6589790Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6590000Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6590560Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6590860Z    /var/root
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6615640Z  - back up /etc/bashrc to /etc/bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6616120Z  - update /etc/bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6652350Z  - back up /etc/zshrc to /etc/zshrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6654110Z  - update /etc/zshrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6654730Z  - create a Nix volume and a LaunchDaemon to mount it
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6655860Z  - create a LaunchDaemon (at /Library/LaunchDaemons/org.nixos.nix-daemon.plist) for nix-daemon
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6656290Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6656590Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6656890Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6692570Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6693280Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6714150Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6714670Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6715010Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6715170Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6715310Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6715520Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6715670Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6716010Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6716180Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6716260Z If you would like to
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6716440Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6716580Z 
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6716740Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-25T02:36:54.6717060Z   $ sh ./install-nix
